        "text": "Context: What is Amazon Elastic Container Service? Heading: Terminology and components Function: explanation Text: Amazon ECS Managed Instances is a compute option for Amazon ECS that enables you to run containerized workloads on a range of Amazon EC2 instance types while offloading infrastructure management to AWS. With Amazon ECS Managed Instances, you can access specific compute capabilities such as GPU acceleration, specific CPU architectures, high network performance, and specialized instances types, while AWS handles provisioning, patching, scaling, and maintenance of the underlying infrastructure.",
